          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Playing with Constructions"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.119,
            0.831,
            0.185
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "You will have to open up the compass against a ruler (see Fig. 8.2) such that the distance between the tip of the compass and the pencil is 4 cm."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.197,
            0.469,
            0.22
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Now, try to get the full curve."
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.231,
            0.806,
            0.254
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Hint: Keep the point of the compass fixed moving only the pencil."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.26,
            0.588,
            0.281
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What is the shape of the curve? It is a circle!"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.284,
            0.831,
            0.35
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Take a point on the circle. What will be its distance from P—equal to 4 cm, less than 4 cm or greater than 4 cm? Similarly, what will be the distance between P and another point on the circle?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.352,
            0.831,
            0.42
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "As shown in the figure, the point P is called the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "centre",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " of the circle and the distance between the centre and any point on the circle is called the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "radius",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " of the circle."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.233,
            0.424,
            0.693,
            0.704
          ],
          "content": [
